@@ -0,0 +1,93 @@
+# Why nightly-review never reported anything
+
+## Diagnosis
+
+The job was running. `launchctl-print.txt` shows `runs = 6` and `last exit code = 1`,
+which matches the six failures in `Library/Logs/nightly-review.err`. The problem was
+never that launchd didn't fire.
+
+Two bugs stacked:
+
+1. **The agent could not run: `Not logged in · Please run /login`.** `claude -p`
+   failed on every run (exit 1). The plist's `EnvironmentVariables` sets only `PATH`,
+   with no `USER`. Under launchd the CLI could not find its login, which is the case the
+   colleague note describes. The snapshot shows the error but not the root cause, so
+   treat `USER` as the likely fix and confirm it with the verification steps below.
+2. **The failure reporter never ran: `read-only variable: status`.** The script
+   assigned `status=$?`. In zsh, `status` is a read-only alias of `$?`, so the
+   assignment at line 19 kills the script. It sits between the agent call and the
+   Telegram failure notice, so the failure is swallowed silently. I reproduced this in a
+   scratch HOME with the original script: the error appears and no notification is
+   sent.
+
+Together these produce perfect silence: the job fails, and the only thing that could
+report the failure is killed before it speaks.
+
+## What changed
+
+- `bin/nightly-review.zsh`
+  - `status` renamed to `rc`, and the failure check now sits directly after the agent call.
+  - Agent stderr goes to a per-day `.err` file. The failure message includes its tail, so
+    the reason reaches your phone.
+  - An exit 0 with an empty report counts as a failure.
+  - Each run appends `rc`, duration in seconds, and output bytes to
+    `Library/Logs/nightly-review-runs.log`.
+  - `< /dev/null` on the `claude` call (defensive; see below).
+  - If the notifier itself fails, the script exits non-zero instead of pretending success.
+- `Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist`: added `USER` = `vk` under
+  `EnvironmentVariables`. The plist paths use `/Users/vk`, so `vk` is my best guess for
+  the account name. Confirm it with `id -un` on the Mac.
+
+## Which parts of the colleague's note applied
+
+- **Applied:** `status` is read-only in zsh and kills the script, which silenced the
+  failure notice. This was the main bug.
+- **Applied:** check `launchctl print` first. It showed runs and exit code, and the
+  `.err` log showed the real error.
+- **Applied:** `USER` missing from the plist → "Not logged in" → set `USER`.
+- **Applied:** log each run's duration, and treat empty output as failure, so a green
+  exit code with nothing done is caught.
+- **Applied:** put the failure notification directly after the failure path.
+- **Did not apply:** the stdin/prompt bug ("Input must be provided…"). The logs don't show
+  it, and the prompt is passed as an argument. The original script never got that far.
+  I kept the prompt as an argument and added `< /dev/null` only as defensive hardening.
+- **Not verified:** the external article and the claim that launchd does not pass
+  `USER`. I did not fetch them.
+
+## What I could not verify here
+
+I cannot run launchd or call your real `claude` and Telegram from this snapshot. Both
+fixes are verified only by a local simulation: a scratch HOME with fake `claude` and
+`notify.sh` (failure, success, empty-output, and notifier-failure cases all behave as
+intended), plus `plutil -lint` and `zsh -n`. The real test is on your Mac.
+
+## Steps on your Mac
+
+```sh
+# copy the fixed files from the snapshot into place
+cp bin/nightly-review.zsh ~/bin/nightly-review.zsh
+cp Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist ~/Library/LaunchAgents/
+
+# reload the plist so launchd picks up the new environment
+launchctl bootout gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist
+launchctl bootstrap gui/$UID ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.vk.nightly-review.plist
+
+# run it now
+launchctl kickstart -k gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review
+```
+
+Then check all three:
+
+1. `launchctl print gui/$UID/com.vk.nightly-review` → `last exit code = 0`.
+2. `tail ~/Library/Logs/nightly-review-runs.log` → a new line with `rc=0`, a plausible
+   `seconds` (not 0–3), and `bytes` > 0. The report file
+   `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review-<today>.md` exists and is fresh.
+3. You received the "done" message on Telegram.
+
+If it still says "Not logged in", `USER` was not the only cause. Check that `claude`
+can log in non-interactively from launchd; `claude setup-token` may help, but keep any
+token in the keychain, not in the plist.
+
+To test the failure path, temporarily make the job fail (for example, point `REPO` at a
+missing directory with a bogus value), kickstart it, and confirm the "FAILED" message
+arrives on Telegram. Then restore the file.
